#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1116
msgid "Turn it on in Contact → Form Steps or in the form's Steps tab. The submit button becomes Review. After Review the visitor sees the answers with Back and Send buttons. Required fields are checked first, exactly as Contact Form 7 does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1120
msgid "In place or summary table"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1121
msgid "In place keeps your form and theme design and swaps every field for its answer. Summary table hides the form and shows the answers as a two-column table. Choose it in the form's Steps tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1125
msgid "Renaming labels in the summary table"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1126
msgid "The table finds the label written next to each field, for example \"Your name\" in <label> Your name [text your-name] </label>. In the Steps tab, the table \"Rename labels in the summary table\" lists every field with the label found. Type a new name to replace it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1131
msgid "Set site-wide texts in the Defaults tab. Each form can override them in its Steps tab. An empty box always means \"use the default\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1136
msgid "Choose Theme default, Filled, Outline or Rounded buttons, their colors, their position (left, centre, right, full width, or Back left and Send right), their order, and whether Back and Previous are shown. Set site-wide choices in the Defaults tab; each form can override them in its Steps tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1140
msgid "Form styles and your own CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1141
msgid "Choose a built-in Form style (Navy, Teal, Warm, Sky or Dark card) in the form's Steps tab → Design, and set the button colors there. For anything more, use WordPress's Additional CSS: .wpcf7 form.svfs-id-12 targets the form with ID 12. The reference below lists every class."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1146
msgid "Choose \"Thank-you screen\" under After sending. Start from one of four templates, edit the HTML, and check the live preview. Write a field name in square brackets, for example [your-name], to show what the visitor sent. \"Create with AI\" copies a prompt with all classes and fields for ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1151
msgid "Forms split with [step] tags show their progress at the top: numbered steps with titles, a bar with \"Step 1 of 3\", or nothing. When the confirm screen is on, it is the last step."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1156
msgid "Keep Contact Form 7's message below the form, replace the whole form with a thank-you screen, or send the visitor to another page. The email is always sent first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin-page.php:1167
